{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have RNA-only (config_002: acc 0.520) and multimodal (config_051: acc 0.532) results, but no image-only baseline. The ~1.2% multimodal improvement is small and its source is ambiguous: the image may be contributing genuine signal, or the model may be relying primarily on RNA with the image adding noise. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) directly complements config_002 to complete the single-modality baseline pair, isolating the image encoder's independent predictive power. This is the highest-information experiment under budget because: (1) it clarifies whether the image modality is worth investing further experiments in, (2) it tells us whether the small multimodal gain reflects real complementary information or a marginal effect, and (3) it is a clean single-variable comparison (swap RNA→image) that avoids confounding with profile, aggregation, or fusion changes. Without this baseline, subsequent multiprofile or aggregation experiments would be harder to interpret."
}

